    <node id="sym:repo2graph/graph.py::parse_all">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/graph.py::parse_all</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">parse_all</data>
      <data key="d9">parse_all</data>
      <data key="d10">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/graph.py</data>
      <data key="d5">python</data>
      <data key="d11">192</data>
      <data key="d12">209</data>
      <data key="d13">def parse_all(files, jobs: int):</data>
      <data key="d14">Read and parse every file, in discovery order, across `jobs` processes.

    tree-sitter parsing is CPU bound and dominates a large build, so this is
    the difference between one core and all of them. Order is preserved, which
    keeps node ids and edge order identical to a serial run.</data>
      <data key="d4">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="2792.52" y="2522.00" width="98.75" height="32.50" />
