      <data key="d5">python</data>
      <data key="d11">48</data>
      <data key="d12">84</data>
      <data key="d13">def _glob_re(pattern: str) -&gt; re.Pattern:</data>
      <data key="d14">Translate a glob into a regex matched against the whole relative path.

    Path.match cannot do this: it treats "**" as a plain "*" and anchors on the
    right, so "**/*.py" misses top-level files.  Here "**" spans directories,
    and a pattern with no "/" matches the basename at any depth so that "*.py"
    keeps working.</data>
      <data key="d4">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="1637.54" y="2059.25" width="91.80" height="33.15" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
